  "base_commit": "e52d4caf728186c74354dcc43d63795be453bde2",
  "pr_number": 6095,
  "issue_number": 6077,
  "issue_title": "Ward of Bones: relative-quantity per-player cast prohibition + 'same is true' spell-type widening not parsed",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`Ward of Bones`'s per-player prohibitions \u2014\n\n```\nEach opponent who controls more creatures than you can't cast creature spells. The same is true for artifacts and enchantments.\nEach opponent who controls more lands than you can't play lands.\n```\n\n(Oracle text verified against the Scryfall API, `oracle_id: c3ea1497-63ac-46bb-95e9-d98b93a880b3`) \u2014 are not modeled by the parser today. No test or dispatch branch references the card, and it isn't in the \"claimed parse impact\" list of any merged PR.\n\nRoot cause: `parse_per_player_conditional_prohibition` (`crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_static/restriction.rs`) is the single handler for the CR 101.2 \"Each [scope] who [did X] can't [Y]\" class (Angelic Arbiter is the existing member), but its per-player predicate is a fixed 3-arm `alt()` of **turn-activity** predicates only (`attacked with a creature this turn`, `attacked you ... this turn`, `cast a spell this turn`). Ward of Bones's predicate is a **relative permanent-count comparison** (\"controls more creatures than you\") \u2014 a different axis the fixed `alt()` doesn't reach, so the whole line falls through to `Unimplemented`.\n\nThis is the same *class* of gap PR #5406 fixed for the chosen-type static family (a hardcoded fixed-arm matcher missing a reachable-but-unmodeled variant) \u2014 here the fixed arm is the per-player *condition*, and the same static also needs the \"The same is true for X and Y\" compound-clause widening PR #5789 generalized for type-changing statics, but applied to a spell-type-restriction static instead.\n\n## Fix approach\n\n- Add a `parse_controls_more_than_you_condition` per-player condition arm, built from **already-wired** primitives: `ParsedCondition::QuantityComparison` comparing `QuantityRef::ObjectCount` scoped via `ControllerRef::ScopedPlayer` (the affected candidate \u2014 CR 115.10) against the same count scoped via `ControllerRef::You` (the source's actual controller, per `game::quantity::resolve_quantity_scoped`'s documented split). No new `ParsedCondition` variant, no new evaluator arm \u2014 `QuantityComparison` is already generically evaluated by `game::restrictions::evaluate_condition`, and `per_player_condition` is already read at the one call site that matters here (`casting::is_blocked_by_cant_be_cast_for`).\n- Add a `parse_cast_typed_spells_predicate` verb arm \u2014 the typed sibling of the existing bare \"cast spells\" arm \u2014 extended with an optional \"the same is true for `<type>` and `<type>`\" continuation (mirrors `same_is_true::parse_sentence`'s two-conjunct \"and\"-only grammar) that widens the restricted spell types into a single `Or`.\n\n## Scope note\n\nThe third clause (\"Each opponent who controls more lands than you can't play lands\") reuses `StaticMode::Other(\"CantPlayLand\")`, whose runtime check (`check_static_other_by_name`) does not currently read `per_player_condition` at all (only `StaticMode::CantBeCast`/`CantAttack` do, via a different call site). Wiring that up is a separate, slightly wider-blast-radius runtime change (it's a shared function used by several other `Other`-keyed statics) and is left as an explicit follow-up rather than bundled here.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Oracle text confirmed via `https://api.scryfall.com/cards/named?exact=Ward%20of%20Bones` (Eventide, 2008; `mtgo_id: 30278`).\n- No existing test, dispatch branch, or \"claimed parse impact\" list references this card.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-18T06:36:15.000Z",
